# No `register` or GCC asm in decompiled C

For overall semantic style (struct walks, no asm `goto` labels, readable locals),
see **`decomp-semantic-style.mdc`**.

Banned in semantic C:

- `register` (storage class)
- `register T x asm("rN")`
- empty `asm("")` barriers

They steer allocation / instruction order and are not a real match.

Allowed `asm()`:

- BIOS: `asm("swi N");`
- Naked readable Thumb / opcode stubs (`__attribute__((naked))`)

If agbcc will not emit retail bytes without these, park the C (`park_wip.py`) and leave Thumb in `src/matched/`.
